        "created_at": "2024-06-12T01:47:41.816Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I just recently started recording and publishing my very own podcast, Pen and Paper and Popcorn!</p>\n<p>The concept is pretty simple - we take movies (and tv shows and other things), build the world in some RPG or other, and give the main characters to our players*. Then we roll the dice and see how things play out! Sometimes it stays pretty similar to how the movie went, other times it veers off dramatically.</p>\n<p>We’ve just finished our game of Hellboy, using Masks as the RPG, and I figured that might appeal to a few of you here! Anyway, if that sounds like fun, check out Pen and Paper and Popcorn, it’s available pretty anywhere people get podcasts.</p>\n<p>*Yeah, the concept was inspired by the podcasts Film Reroll and Adventure OSN, which are also great</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2024-06-12T01:47:41.816Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 47,
